# KWarner preview PDF (program report printout)

When the user asks for **PDF creation, PDF updates, printout layout, or program-report print changes**, work in the **KWarner locked preview pipeline** — not the web UI unless they explicitly ask for web.

## Pipeline (source of truth)

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| Renderer | `server/pdf/renderProgramReportKwarnerLockedPreview.js` |
| Shared draw helpers | `server/pdf/drawSeminar.js`, `server/pdf/drawFrame.js` |
| Macro signal data | `js/foodPlanPrintout.js` |
| Payload | `js/programReportPrintout.js` + `js/kwarnerLockedPreviewFixtures.js` |

## Mandatory after every PDF change

1. Run **`npm run render:kwarner-preview`**
2. Script writes **two new files** (never overwrites):
   - **Primary:** `docs/samples/kwarner-locked-preview-kristi-N.pdf` (N increments: …-9, …-10, …)
   - **Archive:** `docs/samples/kwarner-preview-kristi-veg-fruit-vN.pdf`
3. Copy primary file to `/opt/cursor/artifacts/` when that folder exists.
4. Commit new PDFs + `js/kwarnerPreviewBuild.js`.

## What to give the user

**Give them the downloadable FILE — not a website URL.**

In the response, state the exact filename and workspace path, e.g.:

> **Download:** `kwarner-locked-preview-kristi-10.pdf`  
> Path: `docs/samples/kwarner-locked-preview-kristi-10.pdf`

The user downloads the file from the **Cursor agent files / artifacts panel** in this run. Do **not** send `burnandbuilddiet.com` links or GitHub raw URLs unless they explicitly ask for a hosted link.
